  "sections": {
    "work": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "The second boy, a cardsharp, has extra cards tucked in his belt behind his back, out of sight of the mark but not the viewer, and a sinister older man is peering over the dupe's shoulder and signaling to his young accomplice.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "The Cardsharps",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Cardsharps",
          "accessed": "2026-11-04",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "The composition is balanced, the three figures bound together by the common drama, yet each with his own unique interaction within the image as a whole",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "The Cardsharps",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Cardsharps",
          "accessed": "2026-11-04",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      }
    ],
    "moment": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "The Cardsharps, with its mixture of brutal low-life realism and luminous Venetian delicacy, was much admired",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "The Cardsharps",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Cardsharps",
          "accessed": "2026-11-04",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Caravaggio came to the notice of the prominent collector Cardinal Francesco Maria del Monte, who purchased Cardsharps and became the artist's first important patron, giving him lodgings in his Palazzo Madama behind the Piazza Navona",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "The Cardsharps",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Cardsharps",
          "accessed": "2026-11-04",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      }
    ],
    "matters": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "for if the innocent is being duped, the other boy is no older, another innocent being corrupted even as he cheats his gull.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
